MODIFICATIONS
==============================================================================

Every file inherited from the upstream projects has been changed by MARVEL:
the package was renamed (`tradingagents` -> `marvel`), and imports, packaging,
entry points and paths were rewritten throughout. This blanket statement is the
prominent change notice required by Section 4(b) of the Apache License,
Version 2.0; the substantive changes are enumerated below and in
CHANGES_FROM_UPSTREAM.md.

Inherited from TradingAgents-Astock (v0.2.13):
  - A-stock (China mainland) data layer using mootdx, Tencent Finance,
    Eastmoney and other direct HTTP sources (akshare was removed in v0.2.5)
  - Three A-stock specific analyst agents (Policy, Hot Money, Lockup)
  - A-stock trading constraints (T+1, price limits, lot sizes) in Trader and PM
  - Chinese language output support
  - CSI 300 benchmark for alpha calculation (replacing SPY)
  - Various prompt and pipeline adaptations for A-share market specifics

Ported from TradingAgents-Astock v0.5.17:
  - Look-ahead guard: date-aware tools forward curr_date and
    get_profit_forecast requires it, so forecasts for a historical analysis
    date are flagged rather than presented as known facts
  - Market guard: HK/US tickers are rejected instead of being silently queried
    as A-shares
  - Beijing Stock Exchange 920xxx routing, and BSE trading-rule wording in the
    trader and portfolio-manager prompts
  - Stale daily K-line detection with Sina supplementation; mootdx server
    probing and a resilient call wrapper
  - Full Chinese 5-tier rating parser (Chinese vocabulary, Chinese labels and
    mixed Chinese-label/English-value forms)
  - llm_clients/capabilities.py: model-capability dispatch for structured output
  - Removal of executable price levels (entry price, stop loss, position size,
    price target) from the trader and portfolio-manager schemas
  - web/stock_display.py: bare stock codes render as "code name"
  - Incomplete-task index so an interrupted run can be resumed

Extracted from TradingAgents-AShare (PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0):
  - A-share trading calendar and intraday market phase, reworked to fetch the
    calendar over MARVEL's direct-HTTP path instead of adding an akshare
    dependency
  - Volume Price Analyst: the Wyckoff / Anna Coulling analytical framework,
    rewritten as a MARVEL-native synchronous node and extended with A-share
    specifics (T+1, price limits, 量在价先, turnover)
  - Macro Analyst: sector-rotation and policy-transmission role, rebuilt on
    MARVEL's existing industry-comparison / concept-block / northbound tools
  - Per-round debate objectives (debate_utils), applied to the Bull/Bear
    debate and the three-way risk debate. The rest of that project's
    debate_utils implements its claim-registry protocol and is deliberately
    not ported — MARVEL's debate layer is prose-based.

Added by MARVEL:
  - Rebranding and packaging as MARVEL (package renamed to `marvel`)
  - Web UI: in-app API key entry persisted to the local .env, provider
    auto-detection, per-provider custom model IDs
  - Data-layer instrument context, and analysis-date defaulting to the most
    recent completed trading session
  - One-click launchers (start.bat / start.sh / run.py / run_single.py)
    including batch analysis over a stock list

See CHANGES_FROM_UPSTREAM.md for the upstream modification list.
